2. Training machine learning algorithms using Weka GUI Explorer

I chose the iris dataset for this part of the lab work.

Firstly, I had to convert the dataset to ARFF format. I copied all the data in a text file, then I added the attributes
that specify the ARFF format and saved it as iris.arff.

Then I tested a model with the J48 tree and another one with the MultilayerPerceptron.

The J48 tree is a decision tree whose objective is to reduce entropy. It does this by using metrics like information
gain, allowing it to choose the best threshold at each depth.

The MultilayerPerceptron is a neural network whose objective is to minimize prediction error. It does this by adjusting
the weights of its neurons through backpropagation, allowing the network to learn non-linear patterns across its layers.

